The staleness window measured raw commit distance, so an afternoon of
tracker filing (34 consecutive `tracker: N files (M ops)` auto-sync
commits, zero code commits between them) pushed a doc regenerated that
morning past the 30-commit window and failed verify-generated on the next
PR. Tracker commits move no code. The check now subtracts commits whose
subject carries the `tracker:` prefix (optionally scoped) from the
distance and says so in its output; `fix(tracker): ...` still counts.

